        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quirkydm/{size}/2033_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-02-28T20:55:33.079Z",
        "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/f/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324_2_231x500.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"AoVvwVIE3PiWWFZebws0C0iK4N6\" width=\"231\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324_2_231x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324_2_346x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324_2_462x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/ff1f9faf02dcfed3f7a3cdcc2a4e2c748597b324_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">828×1792 101 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>This game was the most respect I’ve ever given Deadline. The first two brutal turns were enough to make me sit up and pay attention to what is normally a fairly straightforward match. Kudos to the games maker this week!</p>\n<p>At first, the game was out of control, but after taking a quick break in the action, Deadline had few tricks left up his sleeve. Everyone on the team was stacking up ongoing destruction, deck control and card draws. Even without Fanatic’s huge damage output, which Xtreme Fanatic can manage even without Wrathful Retribution, Deadline’s very scary start was quickly brought to bear.</p>",
